{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-da677adb-846b-4827-8831-58c3fe8e239c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4db503093afa82a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-dgnyr0rz/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E003.md","content":"# PyTorch ROCm training support for single- and multi-GPU jobs\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic makes PyTorch training on AMD Instinct accelerators (ROCm) a supported capability of the Training Operator: single-GPU and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs run to completion on AMD GPU nodes and are admitted through Kueue, including jobs requesting the amd.com/gpu resource. It delivers the job/runtime support for ROCm training and validates the capability on physical AMD Instinct hardware.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Enable PyTorchJob execution on AMD Instinct nodes for ROCm: worker pod configuration for AMD GPU nodes (runtime images, node affinity, and any operator-side support needed for ROCm-based workers).\n- Support single-GPU and multi-GPU (multi-replica) PyTorchJob topologies on ROCm.\n- Validate that PyTorchJobs requesting amd.com/gpu are admitted through Kueue and run to completion, using the Kueue quota handling for AMD GPU resources.\n- Record validation results on physical AMD Instinct hardware (securing node access is part of this epic's work; the access itself is an externally-granted precondition tracked in Risks).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A single-GPU PyTorchJob using ROCm on an AMD Instinct node runs to completion with correct training results.\n- A multi-GPU (multi-replica) PyTorchJob using ROCm across multiple AMD Instinct GPUs runs to completion with correct training results.\n- PyTorchJobs requesting the amd.com/gpu resource are admitted through Kueue (workload queueing enabled) and run under the amd.com/gpu quota configuration.\n- The validation results on physical AMD Instinct hardware are recorded.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1, partial): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling — this epic covers the Training Operator side (job and runtime support, end-to-end training validation).\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Requires the Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for AMD Instinct nodes to be in place for the admission-related acceptance criteria; that work proceeds in the Distributed Workloads component and is tracked as a dependency.\n- Hardware access: validation requires dedicated AMD Instinct nodes not present in the CI fleet; procurement or partner-lab access is an externally-granted precondition and may slip the validation schedule.\n- Upstream PyTorch/ROCm image cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream communities; validation pins the image digests it exercises.\n- Shared-hardware coordination: serving validation for this strategy consumes the same scarce AMD Instinct nodes; plan node scheduling across the two validation efforts.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36603,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9897d4d4516b5fdf","agent_id":"a94ae0bee30045f32","session_id":"5032c0b6-6c0b-415b-b4db-8fcaacffdca3","uuid":"037f6894-9e1c-4984-bed5-76ac794089f9","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:37:00.841Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
