{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-10cc7c80-7bdc-4b37-967b-0ab1cded4bcd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b084f10c1a932765","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-dgnyr0rz/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E004.md","content":"# Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for AMD Instinct nodes\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers amd.com/gpu quota handling in the Distributed Workloads (Kueue) queueing layer so that jobs requesting AMD Instinct GPUs are admitted, quota-accounted, and gang-scheduled correctly. It extends the existing ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model — currently exercised for NVIDIA GPU resources — to the amd.com/gpu resource on AMD GPU nodes, enabling PyTorch training (and other queued workloads) to be admitted through Kueue with AMD GPU quota.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define the AMD GPU resource flavor and quota configuration for amd.com/gpu within the Kueue quota model (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue), covering AMD Instinct node pools.\n- Ensure quota accounting and all-or-nothing (gang) admission semantics work for workloads requesting amd.com/gpu, including multi-GPU job topologies that must be admitted atomically.\n- Cover the integration with the Training Operator's PyTorchJob admission path (workload admission via kueue.x-k8s.io labels/queues).\n- Validate quota behavior on (or representative of) AMD Instinct node pools: admission within quota, denial over quota, and pending workloads reported per queue.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Kueue quota configuration handles the amd.com/gpu resource: workloads requesting amd.com/gpu are admitted when quota is available and denied (left pending) when quota is exhausted.\n- All-or-nothing admission is preserved for multi-GPU jobs requesting amd.com/gpu: a job is admitted only when all its GPUs can be accounted for.\n- PyTorchJobs submitted through the Training Operator with kueue.x-k8s.io queue labels are admitted through a ClusterQueue/LocalQueue carrying amd.com/gpu quota.\n- Quota behavior is validated with recorded results.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1, partial): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling — this epic covers the Distributed Workloads side (Kueue quota and admission handling for the amd.com/gpu resource).\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Full end-to-end validation against physical AMD Instinct nodes depends on the same externally-granted hardware access as the rest of the strategy; quota semantics can be validated on representative node pools in the interim.\n- Out of scope per the strategy: AMD GPU sharing/partitioning support (no time-slicing equivalent for amd.com/gpu is attempted).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":37353,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9897d4d4516b5fdf","agent_id":"a94ae0bee30045f32","session_id":"5032c0b6-6c0b-415b-b4db-8fcaacffdca3","uuid":"43174144-b08e-4e2a-ae66-33bc435d5eb8","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:37:10.453Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
