del list, matching the productized ROCm serving runtime's supported model list exactly.\n- Published documentation covers PyTorch ROCm training configuration, including Kueue admission with amd.com/gpu quota.\n- The content is technically reviewed against the implemented and validated capabilities (serving runtime, training support, and quota handling) before publication.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-4 (P2): Documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and the validated model list.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The validated model list is only as final as the validation campaign's outcome; if the campaign no-goes, this epic documents the negative result and the supported-hardware statement changes accordingly.\n- Priority note: this epic's priority derives from the strategy's overall priority (Major → P1) per the docs-authoring priority exception, not from HLR-4's P2 label; it does not push priority onto any implementation work.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":38063,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9897d4d4516b5fdf","agent_id":"a94ae0bee30045f32","session_id":"5032c0b6-6c0b-415b-b4db-8fcaacffdca3","uuid":"04774700-bc16-4ca9-8a25-68e1989c2cf1","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:37:19.751Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
