{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-974a39234f70236d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n3\ttitle: Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for validated models\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the campaign clears fewer models than the supported set, the\n15\t    runtime's supported model list narrows to the cleared models; on a full no-go\n16\t    the productization epic is removed and only the negative validation result is\n17\t    documented.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 2\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for validated models\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic productizes a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the models cleared by the validation campaign, closing the gap that the platform today ships only CUDA runtime builds. It delivers the productized ROCm build of the vLLM runtime (built and released per platform version from the midstream), pins the campaign-validated ROCm image digests, and declares support only for the cleared model set.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Build the vLLM ROCm runtime image from the midstream for AMD Instinct accelerators, following the existing runtime build and release process used for the CUDA builds.\n44\t- Pin the ROCm base image digests that the validation campaign cleared.\n45\t- Declare the supported model list as exactly the models the campaign cleared; models that did not clear are explicitly not supported.\n46\t- Provide the ServingRuntime support so the ROCm vLLM runtime serves the cleared models under KServe InferenceServices on AMD Instinct nodes (KServe itself requires no code change).\n47\t- Ensure runtime image builds are green in the existing build pipeline (the component is already build-pipeline onboarded).\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- A vLLM ROCm serving runtime image is built from the midstream and released per platform version, with builds green in the existing build pipeline.\n52\t- The runtime pins the exact ROCm image digests validated by the campaign (recorded in the campaign report).\n53\t- The supported model list for the ROCm runtime equals the go/no-go scope produced by the validation campaign — no model is marked supported that the campaign did not clear.\n54\t- Each cleared model serves successfully through a KServe InferenceService using the productized ROCm runtime on AMD Instinct nodes.\n55\t- The runtime is documented as supported for AMD Instinct accelerators in the component's support statement.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- HLR-2 (P0): A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the models the validation campaign clears.\n60\t\n61\t## Risks / Notes\n62\t\n63\t- Scope is gated on the validation campaign's outcome: the epic is rewritten (narrowed) to the cleared model set; a full no-go removes the epic.\n64\t- Upstream ROCm image release cadence is controlled by AMD and may not align with platform release trains; the pinned-digest approach trades currency for the validated parity data (the shipped ROCm base may be older than upstream latest).\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90b3178d6091b204","agent_id":"a4731f30b686527e0","session_id":"5032c0b6-6c0b-415b-b4db-8fcaacffdca3","uuid":"ad7e3e18-4716-44c8-b96a-b901f4