{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1d2f9312f4735b2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n3\ttitle: PyTorch ROCm training support for single- and multi-GPU jobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: -1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 3\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# PyTorch ROCm training support for single- and multi-GPU jobs\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic makes PyTorch training on AMD Instinct accelerators (ROCm) a supported capability of the Training Operator: single-GPU and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs run to completion on AMD GPU nodes and are admitted through Kueue, including jobs requesting the amd.com/gpu resource. It delivers the job/runtime support for ROCm training and validates the capability on physical AMD Instinct hardware.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Enable PyTorchJob execution on AMD Instinct nodes for ROCm: worker pod configuration for AMD GPU nodes (runtime images, node affinity, and any operator-side support needed for ROCm-based workers).\n39\t- Support single-GPU and multi-GPU (multi-replica) PyTorchJob topologies on ROCm.\n40\t- Validate that PyTorchJobs requesting amd.com/gpu are admitted through Kueue and run to completion, using the Kueue quota handling for AMD GPU resources.\n41\t- Record validation results on physical AMD Instinct hardware (securing node access is part of this epic's work; the access itself is an externally-granted precondition tracked in Risks).\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- A single-GPU PyTorchJob using ROCm on an AMD Instinct node runs to completion with correct training results.\n46\t- A multi-GPU (multi-replica) PyTorchJob using ROCm across multiple AMD Instinct GPUs runs to completion with correct training results.\n47\t- PyTorchJobs requesting the amd.com/gpu resource are admitted through Kueue (workload queueing enabled) and run under the amd.com/gpu quota configuration.\n48\t- The validation results on physical AMD Instinct hardware are recorded.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- HLR-3 (P1, partial): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling — this epic covers the Training Operator side (job and runtime support, end-to-end training validation).\n53\t\n54\t## Risks / Notes\n55\t\n56\t- Requires the Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for AMD Instinct nodes to be in place for the admission-related acceptance criteria; that work proceeds in the Distributed Workloads component and is tracked as a dependency.\n57\t- Hardware access: validation requires dedicated AMD Instinct nodes not present in the CI fleet; procurement or partner-lab access is an externally-granted precondition and may slip the validation schedule.\n58\t- Upstream PyTorch/ROCm image cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream communities; validation pins the image digests it exercises.\n59\t- Shared-hardware coordination: serving validation for this strategy consumes the same scarce AMD Instinct nodes; plan node scheduling across the two validation efforts.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90b3178d6091b204","agent_id":"a4731f30b686527e0","session_id":"5032c0b6-6c0b-415b-b4db-8fcaacffdca3","uuid":"ed58a192-69b2-44e1-94c0-463dcbc0e0cf","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:38:38.518Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1d2f9312f4735b