{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c9f4eea8a1b709f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n3\ttitle: Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for AMD Instinct nodes\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for AMD Instinct nodes\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers amd.com/gpu quota handling in the Distributed Workloads (Kueue) queueing layer so that jobs requesting AMD Instinct GPUs are admitted, quota-accounted, and gang-scheduled correctly. It extends the existing ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model — currently exercised for NVIDIA GPU resources — to the amd.com/gpu resource on AMD GPU nodes, enabling PyTorch training (and other queued workloads) to be admitted through Kueue with AMD GPU quota.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Define the AMD GPU resource flavor and quota configuration for amd.com/gpu within the Kueue quota model (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue), covering AMD Instinct node pools.\n38\t- Ensure quota accounting and all-or-nothing (gang) admission semantics work for workloads requesting amd.com/gpu, including multi-GPU job topologies that must be admitted atomically.\n39\t- Cover the integration with the Training Operator's PyTorchJob admission path (workload admission via kueue.x-k8s.io labels/queues).\n40\t- Validate quota behavior on (or representative of) AMD Instinct node pools: admission within quota, denial over quota, and pending workloads reported per queue.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- Kueue quota configuration handles the amd.com/gpu resource: workloads requesting amd.com/gpu are admitted when quota is available and denied (left pending) when quota is exhausted.\n45\t- All-or-nothing admission is preserved for multi-GPU jobs requesting amd.com/gpu: a job is admitted only when all its GPUs can be accounted for.\n46\t- PyTorchJobs submitted through the Training Operator with kueue.x-k8s.io queue labels are admitted through a ClusterQueue/LocalQueue carrying amd.com/gpu quota.\n47\t- Quota behavior is validated with recorded results.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-3 (P1, partial): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling — this epic covers the Distributed Workloads side (Kueue quota and admission handling for the amd.com/gpu resource).\n52\t\n53\t## Risks / Notes\n54\t\n55\t- Full end-to-end validation against physical AMD Instinct nodes depends on the same externally-granted hardware access as the rest of the strategy; quota semantics can be validated on representative node pools in the interim.\n56\t- Out of scope per the strategy: AMD GPU sharing/partitioning support (no time-slicing equivalent for amd.com/gpu is attempted).\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90b3178d6091b204","agent_id":"a4731f30b686527e0","session_id":"5032c0b6-6c0b-415b-b4db-8fcaacffdca3","uuid":"2aeffe51-ad6e-47bf-8689-0e218d1a9fd8","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:38:39.308Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c9f4eea8a1b709f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
