 productized runtime's supported model statement.\n46\t  - PyTorch training on ROCm: single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs admitted through Kueue, including amd.com/gpu quota configuration guidance.\n47\t  - Any known limitations recorded by the validation campaign (models that did not clear, parity caveats).\n48\t- Follow the Red Hat docs content process for authoring, building, and publishing these topics.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Published documentation states the supported AMD hardware for both serving (vLLM ROCm runtime) and training (PyTorch on ROCm).\n53\t- Published documentation states the driver prerequisites for AMD Instinct nodes running ROCm workloads.\n54\t- Published documentation states the validated model list, matching the productized ROCm serving runtime's supported model list exactly.\n55\t- Published documentation covers PyTorch ROCm training configuration, including Kueue admission with amd.com/gpu quota.\n56\t- The content is technically reviewed against the implemented and validated capabilities (serving runtime, training support, and quota handling) before publication.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- HLR-4 (P2): Documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and the validated model list.\n61\t\n62\t## Risks / Notes\n63\t\n64\t- The validated model list is only as final as the validation campaign's outcome; if the campaign no-goes, this epic documents the negative result and the supported-hardware statement changes accordingly.\n65\t- Priority note: this epic's priority derives from the strategy's overall priority (Major → P1) per the docs-authoring priority exception, not from HLR-4's P2 label; it does not push priority onto any implementation work.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90b3178d6091b204","agent_id":"a4731f30b686527e0","session_id":"5032c0b6-6c0b-415b-b4db-8fcaacffdca3","uuid":"68c44bde-4a38-4f04-a884-a60ef69b045e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:38:40.062Z","tool_result_me